<Guide
  slug="how-the-life-in-the-uk-test-works"
  description="Who needs the Life in the UK test, how many questions there are, the pass mark, the fee and how questions are asked."
>
  <p>
    The Life in the UK test is a computer-based test about British values, history, traditions and everyday life. Most
    people applying to settle in the UK or to become a British citizen have to pass it.
  </p>

  <h2>The basics</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>24 questions</strong>, all multiple choice.</li>
    <li><strong>45 minutes</strong> to answer them.</li>
    <li><strong>18 correct answers</strong> needed to pass (75%).</li>
    <li><strong>£50</strong> fee, paid when you book online.</li>
    <li>Taken at an approved test centre in the UK, booked at least 3 days ahead.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Where the questions come from</h2>
  <p>
    Every question is based on the official handbook, <em>Life in the United Kingdom: A Guide for New Residents</em>
    (3rd edition). Anything in it can come up, from the values of British society to dates in history, sport, the arts
    and how Parliament works. The real questions are not published, so any practice questions, including ours, are
    written to test the same facts.
  </p>

  <h2>How questions are asked</h2>
  <p>Test-takers commonly report four kinds of question:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>Choose <strong>one</strong> correct answer from four.</li>
    <li>Choose <strong>two</strong> correct answers ("Which TWO of these...").</li>
    <li>Say whether a statement is <strong>true or false</strong>.</li>
    <li>Choose <strong>which of two statements</strong> is correct.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>"Choose two" questions only count if both answers are right, so read the question carefully.</p>

  <h2>After the test</h2>
  <p>
    You get your result at the test centre. If you pass, you use your pass details in your settlement or citizenship
    application. If you don't pass, you can book again, paying the fee each time.
  </p>

  <p class="note">
    Rules can change. Always check <a href="https://www.gov.uk/life-in-the-uk-test" rel="noopener">gov.uk/life-in-the-uk-test</a>
    before you book.
  </p>
</Guide>
